#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167175 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166938 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74dbd777-f24e-5d23-b495-a56710d71f5a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08055b09-dc8e-5e64-a169-6b8646c97e18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18t-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08055b09-dc8e-5e64-a169-6b8646c97e18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18t-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302508} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e093a4e-16c7-597e-9369-a2860151d355" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a6dc5997-1d4e-5312-9245-798d648973c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-329817" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\begin{bmatrix}12t \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations. Using the method of variation of parameters, the general solution of the equation can be written in the form\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-12t-6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nNotice that we are given that\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nWe'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t} & 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix},\\,f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}12t \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{-2t}\\cdot {e}^{t}-2{e}^{t}\\cdot 2{e}^{-2t}}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} & -2{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{-2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{t}}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} & -2{e}^{t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{-2t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} & -2{e}^{2t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-t} & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} & -2{e}^{2t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-t} & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}12t \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 8t{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\begin{bmatrix}-4t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 8t{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\int -4t{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int 8t{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating the components by parts, we get the following:\n\n- For the first component, let $u=-4t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=-4\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -4t{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(-4t)\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}-\\int \\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2t}\\cdot (-4\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-2t{e}^{2t}+\\int 2{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2t{e}^{2t}+{e}^{2t} \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}(1-2t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, let $u=8t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=8\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v=-{e}^{-t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -4t{e}^{2t}\\,\\text{d}t & =8t\\cdot (-{e}^{-t})-\\int -{e}^{-t}\\cdot 8\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-8t{e}^{-t}+\\int 8\\,{e}^{-t}\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-8t{e}^{-t}-8{e}^{2t} \\\\  & =-8{e}^{-t}(1+t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t} & 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-2t} & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}(1-2t) \\\\ -8{e}^{-t}(1+t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}(1-2t)-16(1+t) \\\\ 2(1-2t)-8(1+t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-18t-15 \\\\ -12t-6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311737 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166937 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d23f2a1-55fa-5398-9016-dc6fbc55c97b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Particular Solution of an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03391546-51e2-592b-b33e-96a0e7dadad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03391546-51e2-592b-b33e-96a0e7dadad4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308770} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4cc6a92-1dbb-533a-bde1-5f5375f2fb88" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311269} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c40bb4a2-ee82-5c62-8098-95674097c15b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c40bb4a2-ee82-5c62-8098-95674097c15b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310321} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa3b02da-876b-5e0a-8cf7-c53cb24cd812" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5ea97844-39dd-5c98-b9ff-e503c4be0f51" :question/math-academy-id "q-336699" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\overset{f(t)}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}}},\\,Φ=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} & {e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations and the fundamental matrix of the corresponding homogeneous system above. Using the method of variation of parameters, compute ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)$ and the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t)$ of the system.\n\n| ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | $5{e}^{-t}$ |  | $\\,,\\,$ | ${x}_{p}(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | $-4$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} & {e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix},\\,f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{3t}-({e}^{3t})\\cdot 0}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & -{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={e}^{-4t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & -{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & -{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} & -{e}^{-t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5{e}^{-t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\begin{bmatrix}5{e}^{-t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\int 5{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int -3{e}^{-3t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} & {e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-5{e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186483355 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166936 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c20cd9a-5734-5129-93db-55f6dc985b3a" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing the Formulas for Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3815ccb0-0a02-5fd6-a641-0b543d3401e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482908} {:answer/id #uuid "5e8d746b-dfe9-5dcc-be99-d1e679811b59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482975} {:answer/id #uuid "c559ce39-ac3e-51a2-87df-019730cfd49f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483141} {:answer/id #uuid "ca3d2e76-22e3-519f-9402-f852a4dd6ecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca3d2e76-22e3-519f-9402-f852a4dd6ecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483148} :answer-field/id #uuid "61cd9d7f-883b-537f-9ebe-27f46e66ca64" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483272} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16ae9b7b-e430-5eb6-90d6-0e5eeb4fe026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482856} {:answer/id #uuid "3bd223f4-079f-5113-98ce-7fccfb02f7de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482913} {:answer/id #uuid "87aef158-5bbc-550e-92aa-2b0e8fec0d61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ$ to" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483049} {:answer/id #uuid "b1855158-6fc1-5207-a4ea-97cf1edf1b7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bd223f4-079f-5113-98ce-7fccfb02f7de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482913} :answer-field/id #uuid "a38c17d6-682c-5e64-836d-d5ceddc931f1" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483304} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09a64570-7366-5af6-914c-e07e6d0e7733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "initial system of ODEs" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482826} {:answer/id #uuid "27d2dd47-075d-5ea9-91b6-1ba9165b5b78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "line $\\text{L4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482882} {:answer/id #uuid "5c229293-3ae6-55c9-904e-4831007a77da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "solution of the system of ODEs" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482972} {:answer/id #uuid "998d1fee-cd59-50fc-a838-c8c38df75103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first shifting theorem" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09a64570-7366-5af6-914c-e07e6d0e7733" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "initial system of ODEs" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482826} :answer-field/id #uuid "cbc02d96-2205-5f54-a299-6c4d0c2021ca" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483320} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08abfa7f-7334-5a09-af09-c786a05ccd9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "pre-multiplying by ${Φ}^{-1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482824} {:answer/id #uuid "192260b9-3443-534a-8130-e929b08ad9cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "integrating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482861} {:answer/id #uuid "3d34130d-4f84-5764-9a03-4a29a245842d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482916} {:answer/id #uuid "90b352ac-d734-5170-912e-b54c1ad16bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "adding $Φ$ to" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d34130d-4f84-5764-9a03-4a29a245842d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "differentiating" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482916} :answer-field/id #uuid "df59866d-4c1e-5c2c-a658-0b6f4acd9b56" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2f885aae-2228-5978-9940-05380822e48d" :question/math-academy-id "q-336714" :question/problem "Consider the following system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nUsing the method of variation of parameters, we wish to find a particular solution in the form ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t),$ where $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system and $u(t)$ is a column vector of functions to be determined. A derivation of the formula for ${x}_{p}(t)$ is given below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)=AΦu(t)+f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}^{′}=AΦ$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $Φ{u}^{′}(t)=f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ ${u}^{′}(t)={Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)$\n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $u(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ ${x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\n\nSelect the correct options in the following reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from line $\\text{L1}$ by {{field-1}} both sides of  the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$ into the {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L5}$ by {{field-3}} both sides of the equation.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L7}$ follows from line $\\text{L6}$ by {{field-4}} both sides of the equation." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ To get $\\text{L2},$ we are $\\text{differentiating}$ with respect to $t$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =(Φu(t))^{′} \\\\ {x}_{p}^{′}(t) & =Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Next we consider lines $\\text{L1},$ $\\text{L2},$ and $\\text{L3}.$ Let's substitute ${x}_{p}(t)=Φu(t)$ from $\\text{L1}$ and ${x}_{p}^{′}(t)=Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t)$ from $\\text{L2}$ into the initial system of ODEs:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) & =Ax(t)+f(t) \\\\ Φ{u}^{′}(t)+{Φ}^{′}u(t) & =AΦu(t)+f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L3}$ is obtained by substituting $\\text{L1}\\text{ and }\\text{L2}$ into the initial system of ODEs.\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Since $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, its columns are linearly independent. So, $Φ$ is invertible. Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by $\\text{pre-multiplying by }{Φ}^{-1}$ both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\cdot Φ{u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ ({Φ}^{-1}Φ)\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t) \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & ={Φ}^{-1}\\cdot f(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L6}$ and $\\text{L7}.$ To get $\\text{L7},$ we are $\\text{integrating}$ both sides of the equation in $\\text{L6}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {u}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}(t)f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186497352 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166937 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d23f2a1-55fa-5398-9016-dc6fbc55c97b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Particular Solution of an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee041e3a-2f24-52a5-bb75-0aca1b12f5a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4e^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497167}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee041e3a-2f24-52a5-bb75-0aca1b12f5a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4e^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497167} :answer-field/id #uuid "257f025c-7aa8-5698-b6e8-90af2e776c37" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497232} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5163d8a-75af-5737-80f1-4aea32343cee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5163d8a-75af-5737-80f1-4aea32343cee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497060} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e897fb2-9841-5b9d-a780-0a38ba920dc8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497237}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3cbf4a14-013f-525c-b169-07b2a7a14f29" :question/math-academy-id "q-337102" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\overset{f(t)}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}},\\,Φ=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t} & -{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations and the fundamental matrix of the corresponding homogeneous system above. Using the method of variation of parameters, compute ${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)$ and the particular solution ${x}_{p}(t)$ of the system.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2{e}^{3t}$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">${x}_{p}(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$\\frac{10}{3}$</td>\n<td width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td></td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "We'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t} & -{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix},\\,f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{-3t}{e}^{t}-0\\cdot {e}^{t}}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} & {e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} & {e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & {e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}. \\\\ {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & {e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2{e}^{3t} \\\\ 4{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\begin{bmatrix}-2{e}^{3t} \\\\ 4{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\int -2{e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int 4{e}^{-t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{-2}{3}{e}^{3t} \\\\ -4{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t} & -{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{-2}{3}{e}^{3t} \\\\ -4{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}. \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{10}{3} \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311830 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166938 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74dbd777-f24e-5d23-b495-a56710d71f5a" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Inhomogeneous System of Linear ODEs Using Variation of Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6d86871-d01c-5231-92db-3b8f225214a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3t+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6d86871-d01c-5231-92db-3b8f225214a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3t+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310711} :answer-field/id #uuid "61d6c572-063a-56d9-9057-94f1a95d8083" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311052}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fc7807df-c4d5-5658-9ef2-4f270abd2dc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-337286" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t)+\\begin{bmatrix}3t \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of differential equations. Using the method of variation of parameters, the general solution of the equation can be written in the form\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+\\,\\,\\frac{1}{9}$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$23-15t$</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the general solution of an inhomogeneous system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={x}_{c}(t)+{x}_{p}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{c}(t)$ is the complementary solution (solution of the corresponding homogeneous system) and ${x}_{p}(t)$ is a particular solution.\n\nNotice that we are given that\n\n$$\n{x}_{c}(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}.\n$$\n\nWe'll look for a particular solution in the form\n\n$$\n{x}_{p}(t)=Φ\\,u(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix for the corresponding homogeneous system, $f(t)$ is the forcing column vector and\n\n$$\nu(t)=\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nIn our case,\n\n$$\nΦ=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t} & {e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t} & 3{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix},\\,f(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3t \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSince $Φ$ is a fundamental matrix, it must be invertible. Using the formula for the inverse of a $2\\times 2$ matrix, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{-3t}\\cdot 3{e}^{-t}-{e}^{-t}\\cdot {e}^{-3t}}\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{-t} & -{e}^{-t} \\\\ -{e}^{-3t} & {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2{e}^{-4t}}\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{-t} & -{e}^{-t} \\\\ -{e}^{-3t} & {e}^{-3t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{3t} & -{e}^{3t} \\\\ -{e}^{t} & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{3t} & -{e}^{3t} \\\\ -{e}^{t} & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3t \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4t{e}^{3t} \\\\ -t{e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using our formula for $u(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\int {Φ}^{-1}\\,f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\begin{bmatrix}4t{e}^{3t} \\\\ -t{e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\int 4t{e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\int -t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating the components by parts, we get the following:\n\n- For the first component, let $u=4t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=4\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v=\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4t{e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(4t)\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}-\\int \\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}\\cdot (4\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}t{e}^{3t}-\\frac{4}{3}\\int {e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}t{e}^{3t}-\\frac{4}{9}{e}^{3t} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}{e}^{3t}(3t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, let $u=-t$ and $\\text{d}v={e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ Then, $\\text{d}u=-\\,\\text{d}t$ and $v={e}^{t}.$ So,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(-t)\\cdot {e}^{t}-\\int {e}^{t}(-\\,\\text{d}t) \\\\  & =-t{e}^{t}+\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-t{e}^{t}+{e}^{t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}(1-t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{p}(t) & =Φ\\,u(t) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t} & {e}^{-t} \\\\ {e}^{-3t} & 3{e}^{-t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{4}{9}{e}^{3t}(3t-1) \\\\ {e}^{t}(1-t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}4(3t-1)+9(1-t) \\\\ 4(3t-1)+27(1-t)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}\\begin{bmatrix}3t+5 \\\\ 23-15t\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
